Final current-subject closure, 2026-09-28:
The 7,008-object pinned compiler composition is complete (see
kernel-current-composition.out). Its new runtime installs and signs all 848
kernel modules, including test_fpu, through the original module install path.
The linked module body and installed signature trailer are checked separately.
Its common init actually modprobes test_fpu before both unchanged originals:
  fpu:test_fpu       1/1 OK, zero FAIL/SKIP; normal shutdown
  fpu:run_test_fpu.sh 4000/4000 OK, zero FAIL/SKIP; normal shutdown
The observed stress denominator matches the nonce-bound online-CPU count (4).
Outer TAP and nested worker verdicts are both retained. Original argv and
45-second test limits are unchanged; no failure is rescued by retries.

This pairs with the qualified reference results above and closes K12f, not
the complete 970-program campaign or expanded KUnit. CONFIG_MODULE_SIG_FORCE
is disabled, so loading is not a signature-enforcement acceptance claim.

